  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fda61f7768bd1bb4fad2a446bbbc031a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  planets:
  - planetObject: {fileID: 3241770234809151846}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 1279731515}
    planetButton: {fileID: 693896667}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7119349f34dff354c81417f1a12993d2, type: 3}
    voiceText: The sun is the central star of our solar system. Its enormous gravity
      keeps the planets and other objects in orbit around it
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 5776575494649786293}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 671156626}
    planetButton: {fileID: 186114143}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a7322c7a6a6b01947953c06506608bf1, type: 3}
    voiceText: Mercury follows the innermost orbit and has the shortest year of all
      the planets
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 8697675111918829550}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 2082669654}
    planetButton: {fileID: 629846201}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 151318ac1698f114cadfbfbc183fdd1d, type: 3}
    voiceText: Venus follows the second orbit and takes longer to complete one revolution
      around the sun
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 1278856918192839643}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 1804339558}
    planetButton: {fileID: 1067595834}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6db9fddb85e1e584989d8b985578fe20, type: 3}
    voiceText: Earth follows the third orbit and completes one revolution around
      the sun in about 1 year
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 4210295378960980602}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 1372191030}
    planetButton: {fileID: 1174477775}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fd370110d1b996443b7aa5731428a271, type: 3}
    voiceText: Mars follows the fourth orbit and takes about 687 Earth days to complete
      one revolution
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 2796009221653637325}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 756734835}
    planetButton: {fileID: 1770468340}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dfdac931442b32c49b11603906b7836b, type: 3}
    voiceText: Jupiter follows the fifth orbit and has the longest orbital period
      of the inner five planets
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 8730371303678834550}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 970506094}
    planetButton: {fileID: 1526803621}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d9df0bfda5afa6f46aceea4ed1d8640f, type: 3}
    voiceText: Saturn follows the sixth orbit and is famous for its extensive ring
      system
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 675296804779578175}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 1479332905}
    planetButton: {fileID: 958356580}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 46a94e0994465e740838a3fcedf23baa, type: 3}
    voiceText: Uranus follows the seventh orbit and takes about 84 Earth years to
      complete one revolution
    isVisited: 0
  - planetObject: {fileID: 6941456562815172649}
    labelCanvas: {fileID: 1760358461}
    planetButton: {fileID: 510615720}
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b8e5cc5da2ac8394c8a4fb87f325f01f, type: 3}
    voiceText: Neptune follows the eighth and outermost planetary orbit and takes
      about 165 Earth years to orbit the sun
    isVisited: 0
  planetFocusController: {fileID: 745791329}
  solarSystemAnimator: {fileID: 685843351}
  orbitAnimationName: SolarSystemOrbit
